<Layout title="Specification"><section class="page"><p class="eyebrow">ORBIT v0.1 · Draft</p><h1>Keep execution aligned with durable outcomes.</h1><p class="lede">An ORBIT Plan is a portable declaration of durable software intent and outcomes designed to be reconciled against current reality before execution work is materialised.</p><div class="callout"><strong>A Plan is not a backlog.</strong><br />ORBIT keeps intent durable while deriving only the next bounded execution slice from current reality.</div><h2>Execution neutrality</h2><p>ORBIT defines planning artefacts, outcome contracts, acceptance criteria, reconciliation semantics, execution-slice contracts, and provenance.</p><p>ORBIT does not define coding agents, issue trackers, branch workflows, CI/CD, model providers, source-control hosting, or orchestration systems.</p></section></Layout>
